cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DOMINION in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "DOMINION: Domain Identification for Networks of Immunolabeled Object Neighborhoods"
abstract: >-
  A napari workflow that partitions 2D immunofluorescence tissue images into
  per-object domains by signal-guided seeded watershed tessellation, with
  per-domain measurements, skeletons and Sholl analysis.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Garrick
    family-names: Salois
version: 0.3.1
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GSNautilus/Dominion"
keywords:
  - napari
  - immunofluorescence
  - image analysis
  - tessellation
  - watershed
  - astrocytes
  - Sholl analysis
